[Comments]
Lines=7
Line1=Development binding template; runtime CANopen services are integrated but still require target interoperability verification.
Line2=This file describes classic CANopen CiA 301, not CiA 1301 CANopen FD.
Line3=Manufacturer MIT mode -128 and objects at 0x2000 are not standardized CiA 402 modes.
Line4=Q16.16 position is rad, velocity is rad/s, acceleration is rad/s^2.
Line5=MIT gains and current limit use UQ8.8; multibyte values are little-endian on CANopen.
Line6=Replace all development identity values with identifiers legally assigned to the product owner.
Line7=Nonzero controlword also requires configured and active 0x1016 remote Operational heartbeat supervision.

